course: dictionary
lesson: 2870
title: Giving to help
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To donate means to give something to help someone, without being paid back. You can donate money, things, or your time. «A charity is a group that helps people or animals; to donate is to give money to help.» The word donate tells you that somebody is giving freely.
explain: «A charity shop sells donated things and gives the money to a good cause.» Donated things are given by people, not bought from a shop first. The clue is in the word itself: donated things are gifts, and the shop uses the money to help a good cause.
explain: Donate can also mean giving part of your body to help someone. Adults donate blood, and doctors take it so it can save someone else. Here the reader learns that donating can be a kind and serious act, not just handing over money.
fact: Donate means to give freely, without being paid back.
fact: You can donate money, things, time, or even blood.
fact: A charity is a group that helps people or animals.
fact: A charity shop sells donated things and gives the money to a good cause.
fact: Fundraising is collecting money for a good cause. For example, 40 people each donate 50p, so 40 × 50p = £20 is raised.
exercise: «A charity shop sells donated things.» What does donated mean here? | *Given freely to help | Thrown away by the shop | Bought with a lot of money | Stolen from a shop
exercise: What does it mean to donate blood? | To sell your blood for money | To buy a bag of blood | To wash the blood off your hands | *To let doctors take it so it can save someone else
exercise: Find and copy one word from «A charity is a group that helps people or animals» that means a group that helps people or animals. | people | *charity | group | animals
test: «The school asked us to donate old books for the library.» What does donate mean here? | *To give them freely to help | To count them | To lend them and get them back | To throw them away
test: Mum says, «I will donate some time at the food bank this weekend.» What is she giving? | Money only | Her old car | Her shoes | *Her time, to help
exam: Forty people each donate 50p to a school fundraiser. How much money is raised? | £40 | *£20 | £15 | £10
